 "text": "Butler County Recorder\nSkip to main content\nAbout Us\nAccessibility Statement\nRecorder's Bio\nGeneral Information\nFees (Opens in new window)\nForms\nPublic Record Policy\nDisclaimer\nLinks\nContact Us\nRecording Information\nStandardization Laws\nFees (Opens in new window)\neRecording\nForms\nRecording Activity Reports\nSearch Records\nLegacy Search - 1987-Present\nReal Estate Records Search - Cloud Search (Opens in new window)\nCloud Search Instructions (Opens in new window)\nGeographical Indexes - Prior 1987\nOther Index Books - Prior 1987\nAlphabetical Index (Grantor/Grantee) - Prior 1987\nHistorical Books\nPlats\nPlat Search\nPlat Conversion Book (Opens in new window)\nLand Record Book (Opens in new window)\nSchedule of Inlots - NEW\nOther Records\nAtlases - Historic\nZoning Resolutions\nAnnexations\nRegistered Land Certificates\nRecording Activity Reports\nVeteran Information\nVeteran ID Cards\nMilitary Discharge (DD214)\nVeteran Grave Registration\nProperty Alert\nI Want To...\nSearch\nWelcome to Butler County Recorder\n×\nOffice Information\nStay Up-to-Date Register for our email notifications (Opens in new window)\nThis is not to receive Property Alerts\nRead More\neRecording\nSave time & Money.\nSign up for eRecording!\nLearn More about eRecording\nSet up your Property Alert Today!\nProtect your property and help combat fraud with this new tool!\nLearn More about Set up your Property Alert Today!\nNotice of Increased Recording Fees\nEffective January 1, 2025\nLearn More about Notice of Increased Recording Fees\n1\n2\n3\nPrev Next\nQuick Links Toggle\nEmpty Header\nReal Estate Search\n(Opens in new window)\nDocument Standards\n(Opens in new window)\nFee Schedule\n(Opens in new window)\nVeteran ID's\n(Opens in new window)\nContact Us\n(Opens in new window)\nRecent News & Announcements\nView All News\nADA Title II Digital Accessibility Rule - Read More\nVeteran Identification Cards Available\nThe Butler County Recorder issues Veteran ID Cards for honorably discharged Veterans Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. until 3:00 p.m..\nElectronic Notarization is Here!\nEffective September 20th, 2019 the Ohio Notary Laws have changed.\nAll documents recorded from 1987 to present are available on our online search.\nWARNING - DOCUMENTS RECORDED IN THE RECORDER'S OFFICE GENERALLY ARE CONSIDERED TO BE PUBLIC RECORDS. OTHER PERSONS HAVE ACCESS TO THE INFORMATION IN THE RECORDED DOCUMENTS. (ORC 317.42(A))\nSearch Records\nDanny N. Crank, Recorder\nDanny Crank, Butler County Recorder\nAdministration Building 130 High Street 2nd Floor - Hamilton, OH 45011 Phone: 513-887-3192 Fax: 513 -887-3198 DISCLAIMER\nSite By\n(Opens in new window)\nLogin\nShare Button\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://recorder.bcohio.gov/\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\n(Opens in new window)\nTwitter\n(Opens in new window)\nGoogle Plus\n(Opens in new window)\nReddit\n-->\nClose",
